Keep Hub is the shared hub of the MoneyKeep family's Keep and Pick apps: the one
program on a household's computer that the household's phones connect to. It
holds no app's books and no app's rules.

Keep Hub is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
any other software vendor. Its certificates for hub names come from Let's
Encrypt, a service of the Internet Security Research Group.

Every third-party crate compiled into the program is listed with its version,
its licence and the licence texts it ships in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, installed
beside the program.
